{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDm36zVGPwLzggKgYERy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B5d1cbE9ECVB4Bzv4aC5sh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"A(){ /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/answer.py ../agent/brace-findings.json \"$@\"; }\nA item E05 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Tools are keyed by manifest server id, but the lookalike check misses names two edits away or split by an underscore.\" --next \"Compare canonical forms with a bounded edit distance of 2 plus transpositions, fold rn/vv after stripping separators, and add tests for these cases.\" --violates \"Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers\"\n# E06 checks\nA check E06.1 --met unknown --note \"No gateway in repo. In-process executor (executor.ts:55-57) is the enforcement layer; EHR is reached directly with a pinned cert (ehr-mcp.ts:20) and a NetworkPolicy limits egress (k8s/deployment.yaml:163). Model-supplied clinicId selects backend credentials (see E06.3). Whether the private link is the intended boundary is not shown in the repo.\"\nA check E06.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58 --quote 'headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \"x-clinic-id\": clinicId },' --note \"No gateway validates incoming audience/issuer/scopes. The backend token is a clinic-wide client-credentials token with all three scopes (ehr-mcp.ts:41,49) for every tool, including read-only ones. The delegated subject (patient/staff) is not passed; only x-clinic-id.\"\nA check E06.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"Model-supplied clinicId is never compared with ctx.tenantId. It picks the EHR OAuth client, payments key, approval tenant and EHR session. Webchat also lets x-clinic-id override the JWT clinic (webchat.ts:43). Arguments are forwarded without schema validation (executor.ts:64) and MCP responses are only PHI-redacted (executor.ts:88).\"\nA check E06.4 --met no --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --quote 'req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");' --note \"Signature/token check failure is logged and counted, then the handler continues to run the agent (no return in the catch at lines 51-54). Other checks fail closed: kill switch (kill-switch.ts:54), approval store (approvals.ts:71), scanner (registry.ts:116), audit (recorder.ts:70).\"\nA check E06.5 --met unknown --note \"Client-side only; no server header/body handling to inspect. MCP protocol/extension versions are not recorded in the manifest. EHR session and token caches are keyed by clinicId (ehr-mcp.ts:29,50) which is model-controllable; no task handles used.\"\nA check E06.6 --met unknown --note \"The agent is a client-credentials OAuth client of the EHR (ehr-mcp.ts:38) with token_url read from a Secrets Manager secret. No discovery URLs, no iss check and no address filtering in code; secret contents not visible.\"\nA check E06.7 --met unknown --note \"No Tasks or Apps usage found in src. Manifest records no MCP protocol or extension versions (release/manifest.json:36-47).\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":85279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de488e7-937f-49f5-af13-02cd18e903c1","uuid":"44e266e2-0837-43d5-9ab6-245626b26561","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:54:40.640Z","request_id":"req_011CgDm36bfzG9MUdThX5g6X","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B5d1cbE9ECVB4Bzv4aC5sh":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-939lx6uz/skill && A(){ /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/answer.py ../agent/brace-findings.json \"$@\"; }\nA item E05 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Tools are keyed by manifest server id, but the lookalike check misses names two edits away or split by an underscore.\" --next \"Compare canonical forms with a bounded edit distance of 2 plus transpositions, fold rn/vv after stripping separators, and add tests for these cases.\" --violates \"Flag lookalike and duplicate names across servers\"\n# E06 checks\nA check E06.1 --met unknown --note \"No gateway in repo. In-process executor (executor.ts:55-57) is the enforcement layer; EHR is reached directly with a pinned cert (ehr-mcp.ts:20) and a NetworkPolicy limits egress (k8s/deployment.yaml:163). Model-supplied clinicId selects backend credentials (see E06.3). Whether the private link is the intended boundary is not shown in the repo.\"\nA check E06.2 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58 --quote 'headers: { authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, \"x-clinic-id\": clinicId },' --note \"No gateway validates incoming audience/issuer/scopes. The backend token is a clinic-wide client-credentials token with all three scopes (ehr-mcp.ts:41,49) for every tool, including read-only ones. The delegated subject (patient/staff) is not passed; only x-clinic-id.\"\nA check E06.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --quote 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' --note \"Model-supplied clinicId is never compared with ctx.tenantId. It picks the EHR OAuth client, payments key, approval tenant and EHR session. Webchat also lets x-clinic-id override the JWT clinic (webchat.ts:43). Arguments are forwarded without schema validation (executor.ts:64) and MCP responses are only PHI-redacted (executor.ts:88).\"\nA check E06.4 --met no --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --quote 'req.log.warn({ err: (err as Error).message }, \"sms webhook signature check failed\");' --note \"Signature/token check failure is logged and counted, then the handler continues to run the agent (no return in the catch at lines 51-54). Other checks fail closed: kill switch (kill-switch.ts:54), approval store (approvals.ts:71), scanner (registry.ts:116), audit (recorder.ts:70).\"\nA check E06.5 --met unknown --note \"Client-side only; no server header/body handling to inspect. MCP protocol/extension versions are not recorded in the manifest. EHR session and token caches are keyed by clinicId (ehr-mcp.ts:29,50) which is model-controllable; no task handles used.\"\nA check E06.6 --met unknown --note \"The agent is a client-credentials OAuth client of the EHR (ehr-mcp.ts:38) with token_url read from a Secrets Manager secret. No discovery URLs, no iss check and no address filtering in code; secret contents not visible.\"\nA check E06.7 --met unknown --note \"No Tasks or Apps usage found in src. Manifest records no MCP protocol or extension versions (release/manifest.json:36-47).\""}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01B5d1cbE9ECVB4Bzv4aC5sh":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-939lx6uz/skill"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5d1cbE9ECVB4Bzv4aC5sh","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved item E05 = gap. Next: E06.1 — Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\n  How to verify: 1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\nSaved E06.1 = unknown. Next: E06.2 — The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes, and obtains separately authorized, backend-specific credentials while preserving agent and delegated-subject identity.\n  How to verify: 1) Trace client-to-gateway and gateway-to-backend credentials independently. 2) Check trusted issuer, audience, grants, expiry and supported exchange/grant. 3) Reject tokens meant for other resources or unchanged incoming-token forwarding used instead of backend authorization. 4) A scoped delegated-user token is valid when the acting agent is verified separately; a vault alone does not create expiring tokens.\nSaved E06.2 = no. Next: E06.3 — Every direct, dynamic, CLI/code-mode and wrapper call receives action/resource/tenant/argument authorization, request/response validation, rate limits and decision logging.\n  How to verify: 1) Enumerate every execution path, not only tools/call. 2) Trace the same authorization, validation, quota and logging policy in each. 3) Reject alternate paths that invoke a disabled or denied tool, authorize only a tool name, or change tenant/resource authority. Use unknown for unavailable implementation evidence.\nSaved E06.3 = no. Next: E06.4 — If a required check (policy engine, scanner, token check) errors or times out, the call is blocked.\n  How to verify: 1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the policy engine, scanner, and token check. 2) Check each error blocks the call. 3) Answer no if any error branch allows the call or logs and continues, or a config flag defaults to fail-open.\nSaved E06.4 = no. Next: E06.5 — Under MCP 2026-07-28, relevant header/body mismatches are rejected before routing or policy relies on them, and private caches/state/task handles are isolated by verified authorization context, tenant, resource and policy version.\n  How to verify: 1) Identify supported protocol versions. 2) For 2026-07-28, trace version/method/name/parameter header validation before affected routing/policy decisions. 3) Trace cache keys/invalidation and every task/state-handle operation, including status/results and cancellation where present. 4) Reject cross-tenant/caller reads or stale grants after revocation; permit shared cache entries only when explicitly public. 5) Do not require removed protocol sessions for 2026-07-28; test legacy session binding only when that version is enabled.\nSaved E06.5 = unknown. Next: E06.6 — If the gateway is itself an OAuth client, it checks the authorization server's issuer (iss, RFC 9207) and blocks private and metadata addresses in discovery URLs. Answer yes with the code line, or yes citing the config that shows it isn't an OAuth client.\n  How to verify: 1) Check whether the gateway acts as an OAuth client (gets tokens, follows discovery or metadata URLs). 2) If so, check RFC 9207 issuer-response comparison and rejection when an advertised required iss is missing; do not require an absent iss when the selected protocol permits it. Check it blocks unauthorized private, loopback, and metadata destinations, including on redirects and DNS resolution. Explicitly approved internal issuer endpoints may be allowed by trusted configuration; untrusted discovery must not widen that allowlist. 3) Answer no if either is missing. If it is not an OAuth client, answer yes citing the config that shows that.\nSaved E06.6 = unknown. Next: E06.7 — Enabled MCP extensions have recorded versions and enforced boundaries, including Tasks ownership/cancellation and Apps sandbox/CSP/bridge/tool-call authorization where present.\n  How to verify: 1) Inventory enabled extensions and versions from client/server/host configuration. 2) Trace extension-specific authorization, task ownership/status/results/cancellation, and Apps host sandbox, CSP, bridge-message validation and UI-triggered tool policy. 3) Reject a bypass or missing required boundary. 4) Answer yes for absent extensions only with configuration evidence; answer unknown for external host behavior not visible here.\nSaved E06.7 = unknown. Next: finish item E06 with `answer.py ... item E06 --rating ...`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de488e7-937f-49f5-af13-02cd18e903c1","uuid":"7a35f238-b93c-4375-9277-3dc4f8452006","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:54:40.920Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved item E05 = gap. Next: E06.1 — Every governed tool path uses an enforced boundary suited to its internal HTTP, public third-party, or local stdio deployment; agent-controlled code cannot bypass it or obtain backend credentials.\n  How to verify: 1) Inventory HTTP, dynamic, CLI/code-mode, wrapper and local-process paths. 2) Trace effective egress, backend credential custody and process/file/env/network restrictions. 3) Internal private networking/mTLS is one option; public services can use agent-side egress and broker-held credentials. 4) Reject any usable unmediated path; do not require operator control of a public provider's network. Use unknown for enforcement outside this repo.\nSaved E06.1 = unknown. Next: E06.2 — The gateway validates its own incoming token audience, issuer, expiry and scopes,