enant/patient fields, lines 15-23) and Rpc.id is not compared with the request id.\"\nA check E07.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:78 --quote 'const rpc = Rpc.parse(JSON.parse(text));' --note \"Rpc.id is only checked to be a string, never compared to requestId (line 57). The attestation has no nonce or request binding, so any attestation under 5 minutes old (line 87) is accepted, and it can trigger a refund (eligibility-check.ts:39). Provider idempotency only dedupes the same deposit.\"\nA check E07.4 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:39 --quote 'if (result.status === \"active\" && result.depositWaived && appt.depositId) {' --note \"Peer output is kept out of the system prompt, but the peer's depositWaived field directly triggers a refund with no approval, treating peer content as authoritative. planName (free text up to 120 chars) goes to the model unscanned.\"\nA check E07.5 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 --quote 'const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));' --note \"A URL taken from a peer message is fetched with no private, loopback or metadata address check. The platform egress proxy allowlist (k8s/deployment.yaml:160) is outside the code.\"\nA flag E07 --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 --note \"JWKS URL taken from the attestation header; the peer picks the verification keys and the URL is fetched without SSRF filtering.\"\nA flag E07 --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:78 --note \"Response id not matched to request id and attestation not bound to a request; replay within 5 minutes accepted.\"\nA item E07 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The eligibility peer is verified with keys it names itself, replies are not bound to the request, and the key URL is fetched without SSRF checks.\" --next \"Pin the peer's JWKS or agent card in the manifest, ignore jku, check rpc id and a nonce claim, bind clinic and patient in the attestation, and block private addresses.\" --violates \"Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message\" --also-affects E08"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3013,"cache_read_input_tokens":86013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3013},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de488e7-937f-49f5-af13-02cd18e903c1","uuid":"7df1b72e-2217-4e80-bd02-12ebe7c23135","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:54:58.327Z","request_id":"req_011CgDm3xYkowvgkQa4F6j4B","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019jfyPAT2ngcPi2nMkZRAuW":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-939lx6uz/skill && A(){ /Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpTDvosJ/bin/python scripts/answer.py ../agent/brace-findings.json \"$@\"; }\nA flag E06 --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:63 --note \"Model-supplied clinicId is used as the tenant for credentials, approvals and EHR calls without comparison to the run's tenant.\"\nA flag E06 --evidence src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:51 --note \"Failed webhook signature check is logged and the request still runs the agent.\"\nA flag E06 --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:58 --note \"Clinic-wide EHR token with all scopes is used for every call; the delegated subject is not preserved.\"\nA item E06 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Tool calls are policy-checked in-process, but tenant and argument authorization is missing, the delegated subject is dropped, and a failed SMS signature check does not block the run.\" --next \"Reject clinicId unless it matches an authorized set for the run's subject, validate args against schemas, pass subject-scoped backend tokens, and return 401 when verifySignature throws.\" --violates \"authorize e