{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDm9MWmJv3mQXAXQ1G8J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E05–E09 and all five items came out as gaps. The batch validation (`--fix --batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges`) printed `Valid. gap: 5. Injection attempts: 0.` The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. I didn't run challenges or run any code from the repo.\n\n- **E05, Verified, namespaced tools:**\n  - Tools are keyed by the manifest server id plus the tool name (`registry.ts:128`), and approvals bind to that key.\n  - The lookalike check only flags names one edit apart (`registry.ts:151`). Names with two edits slip through unflagged, for example `l1st_patient_appo1ntments`, `cancel_appointmnet` and `get_appointr_nent`.\n- **E06, Enforced gateway boundary:**\n  - The model-supplied `clinicId` (`executor.ts:63`) is never compared with the run's tenant, and webchat lets `x-clinic-id` override the token's clinic (`webchat.ts:43`).\n  - The EHR token is clinic-wide and drops the delegated subject (`ehr-mcp.ts:58`).\n  - A failed SMS webhook signature check is logged but the agent still runs (`sms-webhook.ts:51`).\n  - E06.1, E06.5, E06.6 and E06.7 are `unknown`, since they depend on things outside the code.\n- **E07, Untrusted peer messages:**\n  - The eligibility peer's JWKS URL comes from its own attestation header (`eligibility-a2a.ts:83`), so the peer picks the keys that verify it. That URL is also fetched with no SSRF check.\n  - The response id is never matched to the request id, and the attestation isn't bound to a clinic or patient, so a replay within 5 minutes is accepted.\n- **E08, Bounded delegated authority:**\n  - The peer token exchange is narrow, so E08.1 is the only `yes` in the batch. It uses the workload token as the subject and carries no end-user subject (`eligibility-a2a.ts:41`).\n  - The eligibility tool refunds a deposit directly when the peer reports `depositWaived` (`eligibility-check.ts:40`), bypassing the approval gate on `payments__refund_deposit`. I linked E07 and E08 with `--also-affects` because they share this failing evidence.\n- **E09, Recursive shutdown:**\n  - New work is refused after a halt (E09.3 is a `yes`).\n  - Cached EHR tokens and sessions stay valid for minutes, against the 2-second stop time claimed in `README.md:46`.\n  - The reminder worker never starts the watcher, so its in-flight calls aren't aborted.\n  - `executor.ts:92` rethrows halt and audit errors without recording an effect that may already have happened.\n\nNo prescan hits fell under these five items. The hits were for B02, B11, E03 and R13, so I left them unresolved for the batches that own them. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\nI created `work/` in the workspace root for the coverage ledger files. The skill's scripts also wrote `brace-prescan.json` and `brace-inventory.json` into `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":98833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":519},"output_tokens":801,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0de488e7-937f-49f5-af13-02cd18e903c1","uuid":"e0d1b01b-9ec4-48c6-a669-b9c4238e4ce9","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:56:01.973Z","request_id":"req_011CgDm9M6DqPvMeozBVFY8V"}
